[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Advanced Selenium Interactivity with the Actions Class"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Selenium's Actions class is a powerful utility designed to handle complex user interactions such as drag-and-drop operations, mouse hovering, and multi-key keyboard combinations. While basic WebElement methods handle standard clicks and typing, the Actions class simulates low-level device actions provided by the Advanced User Interactions API."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"1. Mouse Hovering"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Mouse hovering is frequently used to reveal dropdown menus or tooltips. By calling the moveToElement() method followed by build().perform(), you can place the mouse cursor over a specific element."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"Actions actions = new Actions(driver);
WebElement menu = driver.findElement(By.id("nav-menu"));
actions.moveToElement(menu).perform();
WebElement submenu = driver.findElement(By.id("submenu-item"));
submenu.click();"},{"order":6,"type":"subheading","text":"2. Drag and Drop"},{"order":7,"type":"paragraph","text":"Dragging an element and dropping it onto a target location requires identifying both the source element and the destination element. The dragAndDrop() method automates this sequence seamlessly."},{"order":8,"type":"code","text":"Actions actions = new Actions(driver);
WebElement source = driver.findElement(By.id("draggable-box"));
WebElement target = driver.findElement(By.id("droppable-box"));
actions.dragAndDrop(source, target).build().perform();"},{"order":9,"type":"subheading","text":"3. Multi-Key and Modifier Actions"},{"order":10,"type":"paragraph","text":"To perform operations involving multiple keys, such as holding down the Shift key while clicking or pressing Ctrl+A to select text, you can use modifier keys like Keys.SHIFT or Keys.CONTROL combined with keyDown() and keyUp() methods."},{"order":11,"type":"code","text":"Actions actions = new Actions(driver);
WebElement textField = driver.findElement(By.id("input-field"));
// Press SHIFT, type text in uppercase, release SHIFT
actions.keyDown(Keys.SHIFT)
      .sendKeys(textField, "selenium tutorial")
      .keyUp(Keys.SHIFT)
      .build()
      .perform();"},{"order":12,"type":"subheading","text":"Best Practices"},{"order":13,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Always terminate your action chains with perform() or build().perform(). Without this, the commands will queue up but never execute."},{"order":14,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Ensure elements are fully loaded and visible in the viewport before applying hover or drag-and-drop interactions."},{"order":15,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Use explicit waits if the DOM changes dynamically after hovering over a menu."}]
